# Tailoring engine

Canonical lock: `lib/tailor/latex.ts`. Masters parse into frozen segments. The model produces JSON. The assembler re-injects. Fonts, margins, section order, education, and company names cannot change.

- Do not let the LLM emit LaTeX. Escape LLM text with `escapeLatex`.
- `parseResume` must stop scanning at the next `\section{`. Education also uses `\resumeSubheading` but has no `\resumeItemListStart`; an unbounded scan throws or swallows Skills/Projects. `scripts/test-compile.ts` guards this.
- Masters come from `MasterTemplate` in Postgres (`scripts/masters.ts`). The `.tex` files above the repo are seed fixtures only and are not in git.
- Run `normalizeForTectonic()` on every master `.tex` at import (seed + `/api/masters`).
- `fixEmptyLineBreaks()` stays inside `compileLatex`.
- Fabrication tripwire: only `bannedNumberShapes` forces a regeneration (percentages, multipliers, scale, money, SLA — the shapes that cannot be defended in a screen). `findNewNumbers` is report-only, because expanded mode authorizes invented durations and counts. AI-register backstop: `polishBullet`.
- `polishBullet` may only cut a trailing clause when it is unfalsifiable (no number AND an abstract quality word). The doctrine requires a concrete result clause; cutting on the connector alone deleted the outcome the bullet existed to state.
- Bullet doctrine lives in `SYSTEM_PROMPT` and is enforced by `lib/tailor/bullet-quality.ts`. Software families: four anatomy slots, max 2 named technologies per bullet, entry composition (build/fix/team/result). Business families: CAR only — skip SWE BUILD/OPERATE quotas; CS bridge tech balance only when the JD asks for Python/SQL/automation; TWO magnitudes (HyFlex 30+ = one). Every expanded entry carries ≥1 numbered bullet suited to its scenario (duration, count, rows/run, hours saved); the verbatim anchor entry is exempt. ATS keywords live in skills; experience answers the work.
- Employer archetypes (`detectEmployerArchetype` in `lib/tailor/hiring-screen.ts`) encode each company family's screen culture (bank-campus, fintech-scaleup, institutional-grad, econ-consulting, big4, mbb-tier2) for ALL role families: merged into `hiringScreen` and appended to `lens_directive` as an EMPLOYER LENS line. Grounded in official campus-program pages — extend the archetype lists there, not in the prompt.
- Consulting / BA / insights is a different role family (`lib/tailor/role-family.ts`, `detectRoleFamily`). Families: consulting, analyst, swe, data-ml, infra, product. Title+company win before a tech lens. Business families use CAR bullets, keep campus-ops, and keep exactly ONE engineer/CS-titled software internship (`csBridgeEntryIndex`) with JD-balanced bullets. Pass `job.posting_url` + full description. `posting_flavor` + `hiringScreen` (`lib/tailor/hiring-screen.ts`) are first-class — JD fallbacks fill when Reddit is empty; thin cached research refreshes. Quality gate enforces CI framing, bans invented Confluence/PitchBook/etc., flags mobile-and-web / release-defect leaks, and requires TWO magnitudes (HyFlex 30+ = one). Do not seed Excel/Pivot into `targetKeywords`. Verify with `npx tsx scripts/test-hiring-screen.ts`, `test-role-family.ts`, `test-analyst-techniques.ts`, `test-bullet-quality.ts`.
- The quality gate runs AFTER the compression ladder, boost, and expand passes. Auditing the first draft measures content those passes overwrite, so the repair is spent on a draft that never ships — the same trap as `titleChangeNote`. Any new check on generated content belongs next to `finalTitleChanges`.
- Every pass whose output can ship uses the quality model tier. There is no cheap retry on resume generation.
- Generated entries are re-attached to companies BY NAME (`alignByCompany`), never by array index. Company is frozen per index downstream, so a model that reorders its output files one employer's work under another — observed live, with co-op bullets assembled under a freelance client.
- `keepTitleQualifier` protects the trailing parenthetical. The job family may be reworded toward the posting; "(Co-op)", "(Academic WIL)", "(Freelance)" state the employment relationship and may not.
- `bannedNumberShapes` applies to resume bullets only. The cover letter legitimately quotes company facts from research (a "$1,790 in value" package), and scoring those forced a pointless regeneration.
- Workday jobs beyond `MAX_DETAILS` are stored with an empty description, and their `/en-US/` page is a JS shell — so generic hydration can never recover it and tailoring silently runs with no posting to target. `hydrateJobDescription` must use the Workday CXS endpoint; tenant is the host's first label and `sourceId` is the externalPath verbatim.
- Verify the doctrine with `npx tsx scripts/test-bullet-quality.ts` (free) and inspect a real posting end to end with `npx tsx scripts/test-walkthrough.ts <jobId>` (`--reuse` re-renders the last saved run at no cost).
- ATS scoring uses `claimableJdTerms` only. JD attitude words must never reach the score or the prompt. `plainTex` strips `\hypersetup` PDF metadata before scoring (the injected job title otherwise auto-covers title terms). Multi-word terms require all words in the SAME sentence segment; squashed canon tokens match via `CANON_SURFACE` ("restapi" ↔ "rest apis"). Never-invent vendors (SuccessFactors/Tableau/SAS/Confirmit…) are dropped from claimable terms on business postings (`BUSINESS_VENDOR_DROP`) — never map vendors to generic words in `covered()`.
- Structured JD analysis (`lib/tailor/jd-analysis.ts`) runs before generation: deterministic section parse (Requirements vs Nice-to-have vs boilerplate) + cheap-tier semantic labels (domain, work types, posting seniority), cached on `Job.jdAnalysis`, recomputed after hydration. `matchScore` weights must-haves 3x (nice-to-haves 0.75). The ATS boost fires on score <70 OR any uncovered must-have. Uncovered must-haves become high-severity `coverageIssues` in the doctrine gate and feed the repair pass. Lens suppression governs emphasis only: a term the JD itself names is exempt on engineering resumes (`allowedByLens`). Verify with `npx tsx scripts/test-match.ts` and `npx tsx scripts/test-jd-analysis.ts`.
- Master skills labels are canonical: `Languages` / `Infra & Tools` / `Frameworks` / `Cloud & Data`. `JD_TECH_HOME` and `skills-extra.ts` assume exactly these; `scripts/patch-master-skills-labels.ts` renames old masters.
- Skills stay inside the master vocabulary + `skills-extra.ts` canonical labels.
- Projects: 3 when experience has ≤3 entries, 2 when it has 4 (page is already full). Always 2 bullets each: bullet 1 is what the product is (user-visible loop); bullet 2 is a distinctive non-stack feature + tech + technique aligned to the posting. Pick different stacks (`rankProjects`) so two LLM apps never occupy both slots. Overflow drops the last project (`maxProjects: 2`) before touching experience. If the model returns fewer than asked, fill from `rankProjects` using summary + first library bullet — never two implementation lines as bullet 1.
- Email voice lives in `lib/tailor/email.ts`. Do not add metric-hooks, resume bullets, or a P.S.
- Verify with `npx tsx scripts/test-compile.ts` and `npx tsx scripts/test-tailor.ts`.
